  ],
  "keyInsight": "A point on the loss surface and a line through the data are the same object seen twice — descending the surface and fitting the data are literally one motion.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two equal-size square panels side by side. Left panel 'a)': a tilted elliptical loss bowl rendered as a smooth heatmap, darkest (deep red-brown) at the basin running diagonally from lower-left to upper-right, lightening to cream in the far upper-left corner and along the right edge; overlay ~15 thin light-grey iso-loss contours. x-axis 'Intercept, φ₀' 0→2, y-axis 'Slope, φ₁' labelled -1.0 at the TOP and 1.0 at the BOTTOM (inverted axis). Draw the descent path as a thick grey polyline over 5 filled circles labelled 0–4 in white, starting upper-left around (0.12, -0.13) and curving down-right to about (0.85, 0.50), with steps clearly shrinking and a small arrowhead entering marker 4; marker fill ramps pale teal #b4e1dd → #8bd0c9 → #4db7aa → #2f7870. Right panel 'b)': white background, axes 'Input, x' and 'Output, y' both 0→2. Scatter ~12 terracotta (#c8674a) dots with white edges rising roughly linearly with mild noise from near (0.05,0.75) to (1.9,1.6). Five straight fitted lines in the same teal ramp, all clipped to the axes: line 0 nearly horizontal and low, lines 1–3 progressively steeper and higher, line 4 the darkest and best-fitting; number each line 0–4 in matching teal near the left edge and add a curved grey arrow sweeping from 0 up to 4. Highlight the currently selected parameter marker and its line with extra weight. Keep the two panels visually linked: any change in parameter space must animate the corresponding line in data space in the same frame."
}

The second image above is a screenshot of the PREVIOUS attempt's rendered output (not the source figure) — use it to see exactly what broke.

Here is the generated code to evaluate:

<!-- @FIGURE_UI_BEGIN -->
<p id="demoNarration" style="margin:0 0 2px 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.45"></p>
<span style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:0 0 4px 0"><button onclick="prevStep()">◀</button><span id="stepLabel" style="font-size:11px;color:#555"></span><button onclick="nextStep()">▶</button></span>
<label>Intercept, &phi;<sub>0</sub>: <output id="interceptVal">0.14</output><input id="interceptInput" type="range" min="0" max="2" step="0.01" value="0.14" oninput="document.getElementById('interceptVal').value=this.value;update_intercept(+this.value)"></label>
<label>Slope, &phi;<sub>1</sub>: <output id="slopeVal">0.11</output><input id="slopeInput" type="range" min="-1" max="1" step="0.01" value="0.11" oninput="document.getElementById('slopeVal').value=this.value;update_slope(+this.value)"></label>
<button onclick="trigger_descentStep()">Gradient descent step (<output id="descentStepVal">0</output>/4)</button>
<label><input id="showResidualsInput" type="checkbox" onchange="toggle_showResiduals(this.checked)"> Show residuals</label>
<span id="lossReadout" style="font-size:12px;color:#222;font-family:ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace">L[&phi;] = 0.000</span>
<span style="font-size:11px;color:#666;line-height:1.4">Drag the ringed marker anywhere on the loss surface — the fitted line in panel b) follows in the same frame.</span>
<!-- @FIGURE_UI_END -->
// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN
(function () {
  var FONT = 'Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif';
  var draw = SVG().addTo(document.getElementById('container')).size('100%', '100%');
  var VW = 1024, VH = 530;
  draw.viewbox(0, 0, VW, VH).attr('preserveAspectRatio', 'xMidYMid meet');

  /* ── panel geometry ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  var A = { x: 112, y: 58, s: 392 };
  var B = { x: 612, y: 58, s: 392 };
  function aX(p0) { return A.x + p0 / 2 * A.s; }
  function aY(p1) { return A.y + (p1 + 1) / 2 * A.s; }   /* −1 at top, +1 at bottom */
  function bX(x) { return B.x + x / 2 * B.s; }
  function bY(y) { return B.y + B.s - y / 2 * B.s; }

  /* ── data & loss ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  var data = [[0.05, 0.75], [0.18, 0.88], [0.30, 1.07], [0.47, 1.00], [0.79, 1.33],
  [0.80, 1.47], [1.07, 1.28], [1.20, 1.48], [1.40, 1.48], [1.60, 1.65],
  [1.68, 1.70], [1.92, 1.58]];
  var Nd = data.length;
  function loss(p0, p1) {
    var s = 0;
    for (var i = 0; i < Nd; i++) { var r = p0 + p1 * data[i][0] - data[i][1]; s += r * r; }
    return s / Nd;
  }
  var mx = 0, my = 0, mxx = 0, mxy = 0;
  for (var i = 0; i < Nd; i++) { mx += data[i][0]; my += data[i][1]; mxx += data[i][0] * data[i][0]; mxy += data[i][0] * data[i][1]; }
  mx /= Nd; my /= Nd; mxx /= Nd; mxy /= Nd;
  var bestP1 = (mxy - mx * my) / (mxx - mx * mx);
  var bestP0 = my - bestP1 * mx;
  var Lmin = loss(bestP0, bestP1);

  /* ── loss surface heat map ───────────────────────────────────── */
  var NG = 220;
  var lv = new Float64Array(NG * NG), Lmax = -1e18;
